**Known for**: Tor (former contributor), Freedom of the Press Foundation
(former TAB member)

**Alias**: io, ioerror

Jacob is a cryptography and computer security researcher and disgraced
ex-member of the Tor project. In 2016 ten people came forward to present
serious accusations of sexual harassment, assault, and rape,[[source]][0]
ultimately leading to his removal from the Tor project,[[source]][1]
Debian,[[source]][2] and the hackerspace he co-founded,
Noisebridge.[[source]][3]

He still works quietly and mostly out of the public view at
TU/Eindhoven[[source]][4] and has been rumoured to pop up at events around
Berlin in recent years. He is currently working on the Vula network encryption
scheme,[[source]][5] which is funded by NLnet.[[source]][6]

